      1951&ndash;1980 average. The dashed line is the linear trend.
    </p>
    <div class="hero">
      <span class="hero-num hero-delta">&plus;{latest:.2f}&deg;C</span>
      <span class="hero-unit">{latest_year} anomaly</span>
    </div>
    <p class="hero hero-delta delta up" style="margin-top:0">
      Trend: &plus;{per_decade:.2f}&deg;C per decade
      &nbsp;·&nbsp; Warmest year on record: {warm_year} (&plus;{warm_val:.2f}&deg;C)
    </p>
  </header>

  <div class="card" style="position:relative">
    <div class="card-tools">
      <div class="legend">
        <span class="key"><span class="swatch"></span>Temperature anomaly</span>
        <span class="key"><span class="trend-dot"></span>&nbsp;Linear trend ({per_decade:+.2f}&deg;C / decade)</span>
      </div>
      <button class="mode-toggle" id="modebtn" type="button" aria-pressed="false">Dark mode</button>
    </div>

    <svg id="chart" role="img" aria-label="Line chart of global temperature anomaly from 1880 to 2025. The line rises from about minus half a degree to about plus one and a quarter degrees." viewBox="0 0 860 460" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
    </svg>
    <div id="tip" role="status"></div>
    <p class="footnote">
      Anomalies in &deg;C vs the 1951&ndash;1980 base period. Source: NASA GISS
      GISTEMP v4 (GHCN&#8209;v4 + ERSST&#8209;v5), annual J&ndash;D means.
    </p>
  </div>

  <details class="table-wrap">
    <summary>Annual values &mdash; data table</summary>
    <div class="cap">Every value, sorted oldest to newest. Delta is relative to the 1951&ndash;1980 average.</div>
    <div style="max-height:420px; overflow:auto; border:1px solid var(--border); border-radius:10px;">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Year</th><th>Anomaly (&deg;C)</th><th>Delta</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>{rows}</tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </details>
